WEBVTT

00:00:01.430 --> 00:00:05.550
One evening, as I was washing 
my hair in the bath...

00:00:14.670 --> 00:00:19.470
I felt like I was being watched, 
but of course nobody was there.

00:00:22.170 --> 00:00:24.280
What was that, I wonder.

00:00:24.280 --> 00:00:25.740
That's so scary, huh?!

00:00:25.990 --> 00:00:27.570
I feel ya.

00:00:27.570 --> 00:00:28.880
God?

00:00:29.110 --> 00:00:31.870
This is my next divine request.

00:00:32.520 --> 00:00:36.300
That's really scary, 
so do something about it.

00:00:38.430 --> 00:00:44.190
Heaven's Design Team

00:02:07.670 --> 00:02:12.100
The official request is for 
an animal that's watching

00:02:12.100 --> 00:02:14.870
even though it looks like nothing's there.

00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:16.820
That's so ridiculous.

00:02:16.820 --> 00:02:18.740
Well, it's par for the course.

00:02:18.980 --> 00:02:22.180
Maybe it was an ex who was staring at you?

00:02:22.730 --> 00:02:25.840
Please don't say things that really are scary.

00:02:26.510 --> 00:02:30.120
How about an animal that blends in with 
its surroundings like a chameleon?

00:02:30.390 --> 00:02:33.390
Hey, your mental image is wrong.

00:02:33.390 --> 00:02:35.730
The chameleon is bad at camouflage.

00:02:36.780 --> 00:02:39.930
This panther chameleon was already accepted.

00:02:39.930 --> 00:02:43.390
The chameleon doesn't change its color 
after looking at its surroundings.

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:46.030
It's based on the lighting or its mood.

00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:47.200
Its mood?!

00:02:47.200 --> 00:02:50.260
For instance, when a male meets 
a female he fancies...

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:56.190
<b>2 Minutes Later</b>

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:58.030
<b>3 Minutes Later</b>

00:02:56.430 --> 00:02:58.020
<i>That's so slow.</i>

00:02:58.310 --> 00:03:01.120
That reminds me of the squids 
you made, Pluto-chan.

00:03:01.120 --> 00:03:04.690
They also change color, 
but they do it super fast.

00:03:04.690 --> 00:03:05.780
How does that work?

00:03:06.070 --> 00:03:09.440
Squids have chromatophores on 
the surface of their bodies,

00:03:09.440 --> 00:03:11.620
and can change color with their muscles.

00:03:10.580 --> 00:03:15.420
<b>Chromatophores</b>

00:03:11.620 --> 00:03:15.420
Flexing or relaxing them can make
 the change happen in an instant.

00:03:15.420 --> 00:03:17.530
That sounds like it could qualify as

00:03:17.530 --> 00:03:19.920
"that's watching even though it 
looks like nothing's there."

00:03:20.210 --> 00:03:21.930
Let's try it in a simulation.

00:03:27.720 --> 00:03:30.050
Did we have to go this far?

00:03:31.620 --> 00:03:35.080
Well, reproducibility and field 
testing are important.

00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:38.020
All right, Pluto-chan, bring out your squid.

00:03:38.020 --> 00:03:39.380
Coming right up!

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.070
Scrub, scrub... Scrub, scrub...

00:03:46.600 --> 00:03:48.080
<i>There's a squid there.</i>

00:03:48.350 --> 00:03:51.440
It's too obvious that there's a 
squid there. Mostly the eyes.

00:03:51.440 --> 00:03:54.110
And that jiggly three-dimensionality 
looks so tasty.

00:03:54.110 --> 00:03:55.090
No good, huh?

00:03:55.090 --> 00:03:58.350
Besides, why is the squid even in the bath?

00:03:58.760 --> 00:04:02.380
What's the situation? What does the 
squid want to do behind my back?

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:05.830
This strange situation has
 made him oddly rational.

00:04:06.090 --> 00:04:08.350
I guess the squid has its limits.

00:04:08.620 --> 00:04:12.060
Then how about making a creature
 that becomes transparent in water?

00:04:12.060 --> 00:04:14.110
We'd need engineering help for that.

00:04:14.110 --> 00:04:17.080
I mean, lifeforms are made of water.

00:04:17.440 --> 00:04:20.150
Maybe we can just make a fish 
with transparent blood?

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.600
That'll be difficult.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:22.610
<b>Prototype Lab</b>

00:04:22.930 --> 00:04:26.630
The oxygen transporter, hemoglobin, 
is the reason blood is red.

00:04:26.630 --> 00:04:29.370
If you take that out, 
blood can't transport oxygen.

00:04:29.610 --> 00:04:32.670
Then how about forcing the blood 
plasma to transport it?

00:04:30.410 --> 00:04:37.250
<b>Blood Plasma</b>

00:04:32.670 --> 00:04:34.750
Plasma is essentially transparent.

00:04:34.750 --> 00:04:37.260
You could, but the efficiency would be terrible.

00:04:37.460 --> 00:04:40.730
Then make the heart bigger 
and the veins thicker.

00:04:41.450 --> 00:04:43.570
Let's also add cutaneous respiration!

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:46.360
Then it can take in oxygen directly 
from the surrounding water.

00:04:46.360 --> 00:04:47.270
Okay!

00:04:48.180 --> 00:04:49.250
God has spoken!

00:04:49.470 --> 00:04:51.780
Accepted!

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.680
<b>Crocodile
 Icefish</b>

00:04:50.760 --> 00:04:52.680
<b>Accepted</b>

00:04:52.670 --> 00:04:55.310
Let's put it in the tub right away!

00:04:55.310 --> 00:04:56.340
The tub?

00:05:03.030 --> 00:05:06.770
I know it's weird to say something 
after it was accepted,

00:05:06.770 --> 00:05:09.840
but it would be terrifying if you 
locked eyes with that in the tub.

00:05:10.190 --> 00:05:12.150
Oh, we got a follow-up request.

00:05:12.520 --> 00:05:16.670
Um, could you make it so you 
can't lock eyes with it?

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:19.350
Can the eyes be made transparent?

00:05:19.350 --> 00:05:20.690
That's impossible.

00:05:20.690 --> 00:05:25.750
Suppose you were an invisible angel.
Then your eyes would be transparent, too.

00:05:25.750 --> 00:05:31.430
Your retinas could not absorb the light 
hitting the eye. It would just pass through.

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:35.700
Does that mean my invisible self 
wouldn't be able to see anything?

00:05:35.700 --> 00:05:37.060
Correct.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:42.350
While nobody could see you, you would 
also not be able to see anyone.

00:05:42.350 --> 00:05:44.690
You would be able to 
experience true loneliness.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:46.060
How wonderful!

00:05:46.250 --> 00:05:51.320
I-I see. And I always thought being 
invisible would be fun...

00:05:51.320 --> 00:05:54.690
Even if you wanted to prank someone, 
if you can't see anything...

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:57.420
If we can't make the eyes disappear,

00:05:57.420 --> 00:06:01.290
how about adding eyes to creatures 
that the naked eye cannot see?

00:06:01.290 --> 00:06:03.710
Like a single-celled organism in the water?

00:06:03.710 --> 00:06:06.480
That means at first, 
it'll look like normal water.

00:06:06.730 --> 00:06:08.460
But if you zoom in...

00:06:12.150 --> 00:06:14.220
<i>That's super terrifying!</i>

00:06:14.470 --> 00:06:15.970
I-Is it no good?

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:18.220
God has spoken!

00:06:18.650 --> 00:06:20.240
Accepted!

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:21.860
<b>Accepted</b>

00:06:19.730 --> 00:06:21.860
<b>Single-Celled Organism
With an Eye
 (Dinoflagellate)</b>

00:06:22.980 --> 00:06:26.890
A single-celled organism
 only has, well, one cell.

00:06:26.890 --> 00:06:29.380
And you want to add an eye 
to it? Are you serious?

00:06:29.630 --> 00:06:33.360
Simple and multipurpose is 
my forte. We can do it.

00:06:33.710 --> 00:06:35.810
Let's do our best together, Mars-san.

00:06:35.810 --> 00:06:38.360
Yeah, yeah. I'll be counting on you.

00:06:38.590 --> 00:06:42.310
The request was to make 
a scary story not so scary.

00:06:42.310 --> 00:06:45.620
Why did that result in a 
scary creature being born?

00:06:46.000 --> 00:06:48.830
I would have preferred having a cute,

00:06:48.830 --> 00:06:51.870
small, transparent fish there when 
I feel someone looking at me

00:06:51.870 --> 00:06:54.140
from a place that looks empty.

00:06:54.360 --> 00:06:56.390
I feel you!

00:06:57.050 --> 00:07:02.370
<i>"Watching, even though nobody's there"...
Isn't that God?</i>

00:07:03.400 --> 00:07:07.900
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:07.530
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:07:08.410 --> 00:07:13.280
I didn't know that chameleons 
change color based on their mood.

00:07:13.280 --> 00:07:15.130
I always thought that was for camouflage.

00:07:15.440 --> 00:07:18.840
Chameleons turn black when 
they're stressed out or depressed.

00:07:18.840 --> 00:07:20.550
They're so sensitive.

00:07:20.550 --> 00:07:23.870
It's so interesting that there are creatures 
that change color based on their mood.

00:07:23.870 --> 00:07:26.170
I think you'd change color, too.

00:07:26.390 --> 00:07:28.290
Their color also changes based on the sun.

00:07:28.570 --> 00:07:31.160
When it's hot, it goes into 
infrared reflection mode,

00:07:31.160 --> 00:07:33.680
so its body temperature 
doesn't get too high.

00:07:33.980 --> 00:07:35.890
So when it's in a light spot,

00:07:35.890 --> 00:07:40.630
it gets lighter to reflect the sun, 
and when it's in a dark spot, it gets dark—

00:07:40.630 --> 00:07:43.430
Wait? Isn't this camouflage?

00:07:43.430 --> 00:07:47.450
Yeah, often that's the result.

00:07:47.680 --> 00:07:49.400
I see!

00:07:50.370 --> 00:07:52.440
See? You changed color.

00:07:59.240 --> 00:08:00.750
Wow!

00:08:01.540 --> 00:08:02.520
So pretty!

00:08:04.520 --> 00:08:05.410
Nice!

00:08:06.990 --> 00:08:09.220
I'm worried.

00:08:09.480 --> 00:08:11.300
Ever since that big fireworks show,

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:15.970
my grandson Kenta has only been sighing.

00:08:16.290 --> 00:08:18.900
<i>I want to meet them again.</i>

00:08:18.900 --> 00:08:21.930
He was drawing something like a portrait.

00:08:22.280 --> 00:08:25.970
I thought it might be my 
grandson's first love.

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:31.400
So I decided to create the 
object of his first love.

00:08:35.870 --> 00:08:37.110
C-Create?

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:40.860
<i>This situation has gone mad all of a sudden!</i>

00:08:41.200 --> 00:08:44.340
What do you mean by "create"?

00:08:44.340 --> 00:08:46.990
Wouldn't it be faster to 
find the other child?

00:08:47.450 --> 00:08:52.190
Pluto-chan was there, too. 
Why don't you ask her to help?

00:08:52.190 --> 00:08:55.990
Well, I did go and ask her, but...

00:08:57.130 --> 00:09:00.770
I didn't really see anyone like that.
It was very crowded, anyway.

00:09:00.990 --> 00:09:04.140
I see. Sorry for bothering 
you when you're busy.

00:09:04.140 --> 00:09:06.710
What are you working on, anyway?

00:09:06.710 --> 00:09:09.120
A "creature with eyes that stand out."

00:09:09.120 --> 00:09:12.240
I went to the fireworks 
because I wanted to see how

00:09:12.240 --> 00:09:14.460
the prototype for this nocturnal 
animal would react.

00:09:14.460 --> 00:09:16.910
Oh, for the internal competition!

00:09:16.910 --> 00:09:18.800
I might submit something, too.

00:09:19.040 --> 00:09:22.730
The person my grandson wanted to 
meet was "cute, with big eyes."

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:24.120
Sounds nice!

00:09:24.120 --> 00:09:29.530
So since I have no leads, I decided 
to just create something.

00:09:29.530 --> 00:09:34.380
Huh... By the way, why is Pluto-san 
staying in a tent on Galapagos?

00:09:34.380 --> 00:09:36.300
In order to push herself.

00:09:36.730 --> 00:09:38.570
Even though she's in the middle of nature,

00:09:38.570 --> 00:09:40.410
she's not even stepping outside of the tent.

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:42.260
It's like she locked 
herself in a can to work.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:43.810
She's very stoic, huh?

00:09:43.810 --> 00:09:46.310
<b>Prototype Lab</b>

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.310
The base is done already.

00:09:46.310 --> 00:09:48.800
Kenta will be so happy!

00:09:48.800 --> 00:09:54.270
I don't think seeing something that has a 
vague resemblance is what Kenta wanted.

00:09:54.270 --> 00:09:57.370
He wanted to have another encounter, 
so of course he'll be happy.

00:09:57.370 --> 00:09:59.330
<i>I'm surrounded by madmen!</i>

00:09:59.740 --> 00:10:01.330
Here we are!

00:10:07.570 --> 00:10:09.940
I think this is what the 
base should look like.

00:10:09.940 --> 00:10:10.880
What do you think?

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:12.950
It looks just like your grandson's drawing.

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:15.120
<i>I really don't think so!</i>

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:16.850
Listen, about this kid...

00:10:16.850 --> 00:10:18.580
<i>Finally, a voice of reason!</i>

00:10:18.850 --> 00:10:23.270
If the eyes are this big, I can't 
make muscles to move the eyeballs.

00:10:23.270 --> 00:10:25.130
There's not enough room in its skull.

00:10:25.130 --> 00:10:26.850
<i>Wait, that's your objection?!</i>

00:10:27.290 --> 00:10:30.310
Eyeballs need quite a lot 
of space in the back.

00:10:30.310 --> 00:10:34.640
If the eyes are this big, 
they'll fill the entire skull cavity.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:40.980
Hm, but Mercury-san, didn't the ostrich 
that you designed also have big eyes?

00:10:40.980 --> 00:10:44.240
The ostrich also doesn't have room 
for muscles to move the eyes.

00:10:44.240 --> 00:10:47.880
That's why I made it so it moves 
its entire head to look at things.

00:10:48.220 --> 00:10:50.890
Next, we have this tongue here.

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:54.470
Mercury-kun, you made an 
animal like this, right?

00:10:54.470 --> 00:10:55.750
The gecko.

00:10:55.750 --> 00:10:59.180
Since it doesn't have eyelids, it licks its 
eyes with its tongue to lubricate them.

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:01.130
It's sort of cute.

00:11:01.130 --> 00:11:03.900
I see. You mean like this?

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:06.900
<i>Th-That's not cute!</i>

00:11:07.290 --> 00:11:08.660
Chief,

00:11:09.170 --> 00:11:12.430
might this line in the eye 
be a winking expression?

00:11:12.640 --> 00:11:14.930
That suggests there are eyelids.

00:11:14.930 --> 00:11:19.520
Oh, right. Then let's make the 
long tongue be for feeding.

00:11:19.520 --> 00:11:20.900
One more thing.

00:11:21.460 --> 00:11:23.330
This detail here by the mouth.

00:11:23.330 --> 00:11:25.400
Could there be two tongues?

00:11:26.360 --> 00:11:31.510
That would mean there's one for 
grooming and one for feeding.

00:11:31.510 --> 00:11:34.660
I see! Let's go with that idea, too.

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:39.180
<i>Oh, no! Kenta-kun's first love...</i>

00:11:39.180 --> 00:11:41.490
<i>Aren't we drifting further and 
further from the answer here?</i>

00:11:41.490 --> 00:11:43.880
<i>But maybe I should just be happy 
the base wasn't a horse.</i>

00:11:44.540 --> 00:11:46.210
Mars-kun, what do you think?

00:11:46.210 --> 00:11:49.300
Well, what kind of food are we looking at?

00:11:49.300 --> 00:11:51.690
Since there are two eyes facing forward,

00:11:51.690 --> 00:11:54.190
this is not an herbivore, but a carnivore.

00:11:54.820 --> 00:11:56.810
You can tell from just the 
position of the eyes?

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:59.570
Having eyes on the sides gives 
you a wider field of vision,

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:01.080
which means you can spot 
your enemies better.

00:12:01.080 --> 00:12:04.940
That's for animals who want to 
flee from other animals, or herbivores.

00:12:04.940 --> 00:12:06.050
Aha...

00:12:06.050 --> 00:12:07.900
On the flip side, having eyes facing forward

00:12:07.900 --> 00:12:09.690
grants a wider area where 
the fields of vision overlap.

00:12:09.690 --> 00:12:13.020
That gives you better depth perception and 
lets you know the distance to your prey.

00:12:13.020 --> 00:12:16.080
Ah, so animals that want to catch other animals!

00:12:16.300 --> 00:12:19.800
This animal runs and chases its prey.

00:12:22.590 --> 00:12:25.250
<i>Every aspect just makes it scarier.</i>

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:27.850
But if the jaw is this small,

00:12:27.850 --> 00:12:30.270
it won't have enough power to 
tear apart big pieces of meat.

00:12:30.420 --> 00:12:32.390
Should we make it swallow the 
prey whole, like a snake?

00:12:32.680 --> 00:12:36.980
You can make the jaw split sideways and 
remove the sternum to open up the rib cage.

00:12:36.400 --> 00:12:40.530
<b>Sternum</b>

00:12:36.980 --> 00:12:40.280
Then swallowing prey whole will be easy.

00:12:38.270 --> 00:12:40.530
<b>Snakes don't have one</b>

00:12:44.120 --> 00:12:47.900
You need the sternum to attach 
the muscles that move the arms.

00:12:48.170 --> 00:12:50.250
The snake's fine because 
it doesn't have arms.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:52.290
I guess swallowing whole is out, then.

00:12:52.290 --> 00:12:55.070
I don't think explosiveness 
or stamina are a thing here.

00:12:55.070 --> 00:12:58.900
At best, we're looking at 
catching slow insects.

00:12:58.900 --> 00:13:00.510
Insects...

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:03.670
Then this must be a snail!

00:13:06.810 --> 00:13:07.890
That's it!

00:13:07.890 --> 00:13:09.340
<i>Are you sure?!</i>

00:13:10.690 --> 00:13:13.320
All right, that's the spitting
 image of the drawing!

00:13:13.320 --> 00:13:15.830
What do you think? 
Will it be love on first sight?

00:13:15.830 --> 00:13:17.190
It would be for me!

00:13:17.190 --> 00:13:19.560
<i>They've created a monstrosity!</i>

00:13:19.560 --> 00:13:21.980
Shimoda-kun, don't be shy. 
Let us know what you think.

00:13:21.980 --> 00:13:25.570
Well, um, just one thing...

00:13:25.790 --> 00:13:28.810
Maybe it's lacking a little bit of cuteness.

00:13:29.070 --> 00:13:32.980
Cuteness... That's an area 
we're not very good at.

00:13:32.980 --> 00:13:38.450
Oh, I remember Neptune-san adding hair and 
saying cute animals need to be fluffy.

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:41.900
That's it! Let's focus on 
cuteness and fluff it up!

00:13:43.090 --> 00:13:44.530
It's done!

00:13:43.260 --> 00:13:45.470
<b>My Grandson's
 First Love</b>

00:13:45.720 --> 00:13:47.470
It's spot-on, Saturn-san!

00:13:47.470 --> 00:13:51.010
<i>I feel so sorry for your memories 
of your first love, Kenta-kun!</i>

00:13:51.010 --> 00:13:51.980
I'm back.

00:13:55.590 --> 00:13:56.710
Exactly the same!?

00:13:56.710 --> 00:13:57.800
Why?!

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:03.100
We were trying to recreate 
my grandson's drawing.

00:14:03.100 --> 00:14:05.190
Oh, that's me.

00:14:05.190 --> 00:14:07.070
This little one?

00:14:07.070 --> 00:14:09.610
No, no, I'm here.

00:14:09.610 --> 00:14:12.610
Oh, so it's not a drawing of the fireworks?

00:14:12.610 --> 00:14:14.620
And next to me is this guy.

00:14:14.620 --> 00:14:17.720
We ran into Kenta-kun as I was 
handing it a snail snack,

00:14:17.720 --> 00:14:19.190
so the drawing must be of that.

00:14:19.190 --> 00:14:21.880
The prototype was much bigger, too.

00:14:22.130 --> 00:14:26.380
Because the eyes are too big to move, 
the entire neck can swivel all the way around.

00:14:26.640 --> 00:14:28.770
It has two tongues, too.

00:14:28.770 --> 00:14:30.110
Same for ours.

00:14:30.110 --> 00:14:31.630
They're perfectly identical!

00:14:31.630 --> 00:14:36.380
W-Wait, so the "first love" was spot-on?

00:14:36.800 --> 00:14:38.630
And God has spoken!

00:14:38.890 --> 00:14:41.020
Accepted!

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:44.650
<b>Philippine
Tarsier</b>

00:14:39.900 --> 00:14:44.650
<b>Accepted</b>

00:14:41.370 --> 00:14:44.650
Yay! Locking myself in paid off!

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:47.080
We unknowingly traced your steps.

00:14:47.080 --> 00:14:49.660
Kenta-kun's observational 
powers are amazing.

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:52.780
<i>After that, the one that Saturn-san made...</i>

00:14:54.150 --> 00:14:56.660
I finally found you again!

00:14:56.880 --> 00:14:58.920
I missed you!

00:14:57.200 --> 00:14:58.770
You did it, Chief!

00:14:58.770 --> 00:14:59.660
Yeah!

00:14:58.920 --> 00:15:01.630
I wanted to see you!

00:15:00.100 --> 00:15:02.560
I-I'm... happy for you.

00:15:01.630 --> 00:15:02.950
So cute!

00:15:10.430 --> 00:15:13.850
I don't think the ear canal 
should be any bigger.

00:15:14.380 --> 00:15:16.840
Mars-san, how's progress?

00:15:17.060 --> 00:15:20.420
We're working on "an animal 
with good hearing."

00:15:20.420 --> 00:15:23.620
Oh, no! I can see the 
eyeball through the ear!

00:15:24.420 --> 00:15:26.620
It might accidentally come out that way!

00:15:27.240 --> 00:15:29.140
<i>I've seen you before.</i>

00:15:29.140 --> 00:15:31.860
That's why you can't make it so big.

00:15:31.860 --> 00:15:34.660
Wasn't this Kenta-kun's little friend?

00:15:34.660 --> 00:15:38.560
I'm redesigning it into 
"an animal with good hearing."

00:15:38.560 --> 00:15:40.760
Look, aren't these ears great?

00:15:41.090 --> 00:15:44.060
The ridges are there for a reason, too.

00:15:44.060 --> 00:15:48.760
The sound hits these ridges, which allows the 
animal to know where the sound is coming from.

00:15:44.210 --> 00:15:48.760
<b>Sound</b>

00:15:49.870 --> 00:15:52.340
If we can't make the ear canal too big,

00:15:52.340 --> 00:15:54.880
I'll have to improve this area instead.

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:57.280
You mean make them bigger, 
like with elephants?

00:15:58.400 --> 00:16:00.490
Elephants don't have good hearing.

00:16:00.490 --> 00:16:02.770
Really? But their ears are so big!

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:07.010
You know how you cup your ears like 
this when you try to hear something?

00:16:07.010 --> 00:16:10.530
A parabolic shape is better 
for gathering sound.

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:10.530
<b>Sound</b>

00:16:07.070 --> 00:16:10.530
<b>Sound</b>

00:16:08.020 --> 00:16:09.780
<b>Sound</b>

00:16:10.810 --> 00:16:13.960
The elephant's ears are 
flat and have no ridges.

00:16:13.960 --> 00:16:16.310
Because the elephant's ears are heat sinks.

00:16:16.310 --> 00:16:19.540
That's right! They get heat 
stroke without those ears.

00:16:19.900 --> 00:16:22.280
So they can't hear well, huh?

00:16:22.280 --> 00:16:24.740
But their feet can.

00:16:24.740 --> 00:16:26.920
Their feet?

00:16:28.740 --> 00:16:31.400
Elephants detect the vibrations 
of the ground with their feet,

00:16:31.400 --> 00:16:34.480
and send them through their 
bones to their ears.

00:16:34.480 --> 00:16:36.310
It's bone conductivity of a sort.

00:16:36.740 --> 00:16:42.070
When they want to hear better, 
they press their feet into the ground,

00:16:42.070 --> 00:16:44.810
similar to how we might press 
our ear against a wall.

00:16:44.810 --> 00:16:46.500
That's a little bit cute!

00:16:46.500 --> 00:16:51.560
Anyway, this ear is cup-shaped, 
and with the round ridges, it's ideal!

00:16:52.030 --> 00:16:55.320
So that's why a lot of animals 
have this ear shape.

00:16:55.560 --> 00:16:59.220
I was the one who designed 
the base model of this ear,

00:16:59.220 --> 00:17:01.840
but this time, I am looking to 
make something even better!

00:17:02.510 --> 00:17:05.830
<i>When there are no horses involved, 
Saturn-san's quite impressive.</i>

00:17:06.300 --> 00:17:10.430
These ears might be even better at gathering 
sound if they can move freely

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:12.480
to match the angle that the 
sound is coming from.

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:15.220
I see. How about this?

00:17:18.680 --> 00:17:20.150
<i>That's a little scary.</i>

00:17:20.150 --> 00:17:22.810
Should the ear canals stay 
on the sides of the head?

00:17:22.810 --> 00:17:25.430
If they're on the sides, they can 
pick up sound from all directions,

00:17:25.430 --> 00:17:27.440
but it'll make it hard to hear small sounds.

00:17:27.440 --> 00:17:28.930
Right.

00:17:28.930 --> 00:17:31.500
Then let's bring them to the front.

00:17:32.630 --> 00:17:33.490
There!

00:17:34.870 --> 00:17:36.450
This will up the sensitivity!

00:17:36.450 --> 00:17:40.070
If you specialize in one direction, 
the sensitivity will go up,

00:17:40.070 --> 00:17:43.450
but it also means that they have to move 
their head toward sound sources all the time.

00:17:43.450 --> 00:17:46.370
That's fine. This model can turn its neck.

00:17:47.690 --> 00:17:51.050
Since the neck itself grew, too, 
it can also bend up and down.

00:17:51.050 --> 00:17:52.110
Lucky!

00:17:53.140 --> 00:17:57.380
Let's test if this is good enough to catch 
prey just with sound, without relying on vision.

00:17:57.380 --> 00:17:59.390
Shimoda-kun, please be the prey.

00:17:59.390 --> 00:17:59.800
Huh?

00:18:00.600 --> 00:18:01.810
Uh...

00:18:02.140 --> 00:18:03.100
What?!

00:18:05.880 --> 00:18:07.500
I couldn't refuse...

00:18:10.870 --> 00:18:12.740
It's coming for me!

00:18:13.650 --> 00:18:15.630
How did you know it's coming?

00:18:15.630 --> 00:18:17.400
I mean, the footsteps...

00:18:17.720 --> 00:18:21.410
Oh, that. Okay, let's add 
wings and make it fly.

00:18:23.910 --> 00:18:25.320
We're not done yet?

00:18:25.320 --> 00:18:27.300
Let's adjust the ears too.

00:18:27.300 --> 00:18:28.640
Huh, why?

00:18:28.640 --> 00:18:30.050
That's revolutionary!

00:18:30.050 --> 00:18:35.170
You see, ears can tell where a sound is 
coming from based on which ear heard it first.

00:18:35.170 --> 00:18:36.530
By shifting them up and down,

00:18:36.530 --> 00:18:38.420
they can detect a sound's height
 as well as its direction!

00:18:38.420 --> 00:18:40.030
That's Saturn-san's genius!

00:18:40.030 --> 00:18:44.690
All right! Now detection is possible 
no matter where Shimoda-kun runs.

00:18:44.690 --> 00:18:47.170
<i>This is even more terrifying.</i>

00:18:50.620 --> 00:18:54.900
<i>I can't sense it anywhere...
but there's really nowhere to hide.</i>

00:18:59.260 --> 00:19:02.340
Aw, how did you know it was flying at you?

00:19:02.340 --> 00:19:05.180
I heard its wings flapping.

00:19:05.180 --> 00:19:07.600
This is Mars-san's territory.

00:19:07.600 --> 00:19:09.090
Any good ideas?

00:19:09.540 --> 00:19:15.050
Making the flight feathers jagged might 
disperse the sound, and thus lower the volume.

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:16.340
<b>Smooth</b>

00:19:13.340 --> 00:19:16.340
<b>Jagged</b>

00:19:15.050 --> 00:19:16.330
I see!

00:19:16.330 --> 00:19:17.920
Let's do another test!

00:19:17.920 --> 00:19:19.330
A-Again?!

00:19:22.640 --> 00:19:28.500
I'm sorry... I haven't been attacked yet,
but it's there, right?

00:19:28.500 --> 00:19:30.360
What? How could you tell?

00:19:30.360 --> 00:19:32.900
I mean, when it's twisting its head around,

00:19:32.900 --> 00:19:35.460
the ears flap around and 
are really noticeable.

00:19:35.460 --> 00:19:37.100
You're right.

00:19:37.780 --> 00:19:39.620
The ears are holding it back.

00:19:39.820 --> 00:19:41.620
<i>Weren't they the whole point?!</i>

00:19:43.520 --> 00:19:46.500
All right, let's squash 
the ears into the face.

00:19:47.380 --> 00:19:51.240
Then its silhouette won't change 
even when it's turning its head.

00:19:51.240 --> 00:19:52.380
I think that's good.

00:19:52.380 --> 00:19:53.370
<i>It is?</i>

00:19:53.370 --> 00:19:55.970
Then I'll gather all the 
ideas and present you with...

00:19:55.970 --> 00:19:57.630
An animal with good hearing!

00:19:58.450 --> 00:19:59.640
God has spoken!

00:19:59.630 --> 00:20:03.140
<b>Owl</b>

00:19:59.990 --> 00:20:02.480
Accepted!

00:20:01.220 --> 00:20:03.140
<b>Accepted</b>

00:20:03.410 --> 00:20:06.600
I'm glad it's not the scary one from before.

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:11.530
Saturn-san, where did the 
all-important parabola ears go?

00:20:11.810 --> 00:20:14.010
This round depression on the face.

00:20:14.420 --> 00:20:16.520
The entire face is a parabola,

00:20:16.520 --> 00:20:20.020
so it can focus the sound in the ear 
by moving the surrounding feathers.

00:20:20.970 --> 00:20:23.900
By the way, its skull looks like this.

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:27.530
<b>Left Ear</b>

00:20:23.110 --> 00:20:27.530
<b>Right Ear</b>

00:20:24.250 --> 00:20:27.530
The ear canals are facing the front 
and are vertically misaligned.

00:20:27.740 --> 00:20:30.780
So you kept that long neck as-is.

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:34.810
As you can see, the silhouette is the 
same no matter which way it faces.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:40.120
I'm glad. Since its previous look 
is gone, I don't find it as scary.

00:20:40.120 --> 00:20:41.320
What are you talking about?

00:20:41.320 --> 00:20:43.800
The chicks look basically the same as that.

00:20:43.800 --> 00:20:46.680
<b>Barn Owl Chicks</b>

00:20:47.030 --> 00:20:50.730
You can also still see the 
eyeball through its ear canal.

00:20:50.730 --> 00:20:51.320
Wanna look?

00:20:51.610 --> 00:20:53.110
I'll pass!

00:20:54.210 --> 00:20:56.450
The flight feathers have a stealth mode.

00:20:56.730 --> 00:21:00.060
Amazing! Every feature made it in.

00:21:00.460 --> 00:21:02.070
You're really good, Saturn-san!

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:09.160
<b>Brown</b>

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:09.410
<b>Black</b>

00:21:02.070 --> 00:21:09.490
<b>White</b>

00:21:02.300 --> 00:21:05.310
Incidentally, they have the same
 color scheme as the horse.

00:21:05.310 --> 00:21:06.700
Y-You worked the horse in?

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:09.330
Saturn-san, you never miss a beat.

00:21:09.930 --> 00:21:13.780
Yay, another highly-evolved birdie!

00:21:13.780 --> 00:21:15.970
Oh, Saturn-san designed that.

00:21:16.260 --> 00:21:17.890
Let's make you even cuter.

00:21:17.890 --> 00:21:20.210
Oh, but it has that silhouette for a reason—

00:21:22.660 --> 00:21:23.590
God has spoken!

00:21:23.830 --> 00:21:26.510
That's accepted, too!

00:21:25.340 --> 00:21:28.470
<b>Accepted</b>

00:21:25.380 --> 00:21:28.470
<b>Horned Owl</b>

00:21:26.510 --> 00:21:27.900
Why?!

00:21:28.470 --> 00:21:32.980
<b>The Illustrated Guide to Creatures That Really Exist</b>

00:21:28.670 --> 00:21:32.030
The Illustrated Guide to Creatures 
That Really Exist!

00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:37.960
There are these ear-like things on its head,
 but they're not ears, right?

00:21:37.960 --> 00:21:42.370
Yes, just like other owls, the ears 
are in this area of the face.

00:21:42.370 --> 00:21:44.760
So what are these pointy things here?

00:21:44.760 --> 00:21:46.130
Decorative feathers.

00:21:46.130 --> 00:21:46.860
What are they for?

00:21:46.860 --> 00:21:49.170
Nothing! They're just cute!

00:21:49.850 --> 00:21:52.570
Wait, I'll think of something...

00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:55.890
How about this? They look like leaves, 
so they help with camouflage!

00:21:56.130 --> 00:21:58.760
I feel like not having them 
would work even better.

00:21:58.760 --> 00:22:01.680
When it moves its head, they'll stand out.

00:22:01.680 --> 00:22:03.790
Now that you mention it...

00:22:03.790 --> 00:22:06.500
Wait, then why was it accepted?

00:22:06.720 --> 00:22:09.880
It would be better to not 
have these pointy feathers.

00:22:09.880 --> 00:22:12.160
God's ways are mysterious.

00:22:12.160 --> 00:22:15.010
You're so right! I knew it!

00:23:45.020 --> 00:23:46.530
<b>Next on the Agenda</b>
